# Commit / push public-repo audit (mandatory)

This repository is **public**. Treat every commit and every push as a publication.

## Before `git commit` and before `git push`

Run this gate. Do not skip it because the change “looks small”.

1. **Staging check** — refuse to stage or commit:
   - `.env*`, `data/local/`, `data/uploads/`, `data.db*`, `slides*/`, `*.pptx` / `*.potx`
   - Real names, photos, prayer requests, phones, addresses, bank accounts, payment QR codes, live hostnames
2. **Guard test** (required):
   ```bash
   node --import ./tests/register-ts-resolve.mjs --test --experimental-strip-types tests/public-repo-guard.test.mjs
   ```
   Prefer `npm test` when time allows (includes the same guard).
3. **On failure** — fix the tracked content. Never weaken, delete, or bypass `tests/public-repo-guard.test.mjs`.
4. **Push** — only after the guard is green on the commit you are about to publish.

## Out of scope for “quick” exceptions

There is no exception for docs-only, agent-rules-only, or “already reviewed” changes. Public history is forever.

See `.constitution/public-repository.md` and `prior-knowledge/docs/PRIVATE-DATA.md`.
